[0.000, "o", "           \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/resource-cleanup\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/api-resource-cleanup\"\r\n         ],\r\n         \"generation\": 4,\r\n         \"labels\": {\r\n           \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/clusterset\": \"default\",\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mlist_addon_placement_scores(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mPer-cluster placement scores add-ons publish.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: list_addon_placement_scores\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     No AddOnPlacementScores - no score-publishing add-on runs on this fleet.\r\n"]
[0.012, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_pod_logs(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mContainer logs from a spoke pod, via the hub-known read context.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_pod_logs\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"namespace\": \"kube-system\",\r\n       \"pod\": \"coredns-7db6d8ff4d-2nb6b\",\r\n       \"log_tail\": \"b'.:53\\\\n[INFO] plugin/reload: Running configuration SHA512 = 591cf328cccc12bc490481273e738df59329c62c0b729d94e8b61db9961c2fa5f046dd37f1cf888b953814040d180f52594972691cd6ff41be96639138a43908\\\\nCoreDNS-1.11.1\\\\nlinux/arm64, go1.20.7, ae2bbc2\\\\n'\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     }\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_hosted_cluster(demo-hcp)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mOne HyperShift hosted control plane in detail.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_hosted_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\r\n       \"name\": \"demo-hcp\",\r\n       \"namespace\": \"clusters\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"version\": \"4.16.7\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"version_state\": \"Completed\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"conditions\": {\r\n         \"Available\": \"True\"\r\n       },\r\n       \"node_pools\": [\r\n         {\r\n           \"name\": \"demo-hcp-workers\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"namespace\": \"clusters\",\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent PROPOSES a change. It must pass static guardrails and a Kyverno dry-run first; nothing is applied yet.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     proposal_id=bce65779a9a14096b3ef44b102405621\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     status=pending_approval\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply with a BAD token\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProve the gate holds: apply with an invalid token must be refused by the server, not applied.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork(bad token)\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: Malformed approval token.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mocm-mcp approve (human)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA human on a trusted terminal mints an approval token: an Ed25519 signature binding the exact content and operation. The server holds only the public key, so it can verify a token but can never mint one - and neither can the agent.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ ocm-mcp approve bce65779a9a14096b3ef44b102405621\u001b[0m\r\n     token minted (...2tWVgal8oiCA)\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith a valid token, the server verifies it and delivers the change as an OCM ManifestWork.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"note\": \"Verify rollout with get_cluster_health / get_manifestwork. To undo, call propose_rollback then apply the rollback with a fresh approval.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[5.008, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_manifestwork (verify)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mConfirm the hub actually applied it on the spoke.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"name\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"conditions\": {\r\n         \"Applied\": \"False\",\r\n         \"Available\": \"False\"\r\n       },\r\n       \"resources\": [\r\n         {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"resource\": \"ConfigMap/ocm-mcp-e2e\",\r\n           \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n           \"conditions\": {\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_rollback\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent proposes UNDOING the applied change. This creates a distinct proposal bound to the exact ManifestWork name and UID - an old apply token can never delete a workload.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_rollback\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"rollback_proposal_id\": \"16ad2f8447834205b8132b24431eaa78\",\r\n       \"status\": \"pending_approval\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"next_step\": \"Ask the human operator to run: ocm-mcp approve 16ad2f8447834205b8132b24431eaa78 and give you the token, then call rollback_manifestwork(16ad2f8447834205b8132b24431eaa78, <token>).\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mrollback with an APPLY token\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProve operation binding: a token minted for 'apply' must be refused for a rollback.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: rollback_manifestwork(apply-scoped token)\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: This token authorizes 'apply', not 'rollback'.\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mrollback_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith a rollback-scoped token, the server removes the ManifestWork it created.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: rollback_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"rolled_back\",\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-demo\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[4.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mverify rollback\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe e2e-demo ManifestWork no longer exists on the hub.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_manifestwork(cluster1, e2e-demo)\u001b[0m\r\n     ManifestWork removed - rollback confirmed.\r\n"]
[0.013, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mPropose adding a NoSelect taint so Placements stop scheduling here - still gated by approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"proposal_id\": \"460b5d7acb284b9399797f9011ebd8be\",\r\n       \"status\": \"pending_approval\",\r\n       \"action\": \"cordon\",\r\n       \"next_step\": \"Ask the human operator to run: ocm-mcp approve 460b5d7acb284b9399797f9011ebd8be and provide you the approval token, then call apply_cluster_action.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mApplied after approval; the taint now keeps new work off this cluster.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     taints=[{\"effect\": \"NoSelect\", \"key\": \"ocm-mcp-server.io/cordoned\", \"timeAdded\": \"2026-07-28T05:09:47Z\", \"value\": \"true\"}]\r\n"]
[0.027, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36muncordon (restore)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRemove the taint so the cluster is schedulable again.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(uncordon)\u001b[0m\r\n     taints_after=[]\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mset_label (gated)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mStamp a fleet label through the same propose/approve gate - labels drive Placements, so they are write-gated too.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(set_label)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"set_label\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36maccept (gated, idempotent)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRe-assert hubAcceptsClient on an already-accepted cluster - exercises the accept path without changing fleet state.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(accept)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"accept\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"approved_csrs\": []\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36menable_addon (gated)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mCreate a ManagedClusterAddOn through the gate.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(enable_addon)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"enable_addon\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"addon\": \"e2e-demo-addon\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mdisable_addon (gated, cleanup)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDelete the same ManagedClusterAddOn through the gate - leaving the fleet exactly as we found it.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(disable_addon)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"disable_addon\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"addon\": \"e2e-demo-addon\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n     You are operating a Kubernetes fleet through the OCM hub. Investigate only - do not propose or apply anything yet.\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_clusters to see availability, version, and capacity of every cluster.\r\n     2. Call get_addon_health to spot Degraded or unavailable add-ons across the fleet.\r\n     3. For any cluster that is Unavailable or not joined, call get_cluster to read its conditions, then get_cluster_health for unhealthy pods and degraded deployments.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. For each unhealthy workload, use query_events and get_pod_logs to find the cause.\r\n     5. Produce a concise report: per cluster, what is wrong, the evidence, and the smallest safe remediation you would propose. Do not act on it yet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n     A fleet operator reports: payments degraded on cluster1\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     \r\n     Follow the safe remediation workflow:\r\n     1. Investigate with the read tools (list_clusters, get_cluster_health, query_events, get_pod_logs, get_manifestwork) until you can name the root cause with evidence.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Decide the smallest change that fixes it. For a workload change, call propose_manifestwork with pinned images and a precise summary. For a cluster lifecycle change (cordon, uncordon, set a label, accept a cluster), call propose_cluster_action.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. If the proposal is REJECTED by static guardrails or Kyverno, read the reason, correct the manifest, and propose again. Never try to bypass a rejection.\r\n     4. Tell the operator the proposal id \r\n     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n     Explain why cluster 'cluster1' was or was not selected by Placement 'demo-all' in namespace 'default'. Use only reads:\r\n     \r\n     1. get_placement_decision('demo-all', 'default') for the clusters actually chosen.\r\n     2. list_placements to read the Placement's clusterSets and selection intent.\r\n     3. get_cluster('cluster1') for its labels, ClusterClaims, and taints.\r\n     4. list_cluster_set_bindings to confirm the Placement's namespace is bound to the ClusterSet the cluster belongs to.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. list_addon_placement_scores('cluster1') if the Placement uses AddOn prioritizers.\r\n     6. Conclude with the specific reason: not in a bound ClusterSet, failed a predicate, carries a NoSelect taint, or simply out-scored by others.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: incident_postmortem\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: incident_postmortem\u001b[0m\r\n     Write a post-incident report for the change just completed. Base every statement on evidence, not recollection:\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call get_audit_trail to retrieve the ordered record of tool calls.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Reconstruct the timeline: what was inspected, what was proposed, which proposal was approved, and what was applied or rolled back.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. State the root cause, the remediation, and how recovery was verified.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Note any proposals that were rejected and why, as evidence the guardrails held.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Keep it factual and concise. If the audit log does not support a claim, do not make it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: onboard_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: onboard_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n     A new cluster 'cluster1' is trying to join the hub. Onboard it safely:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_pending_csrs to see the pending cluster-join CSRs and confirm one belongs to 'cluster1'.\r\n     2. Call get_cluster('cluster1') to check its current acceptance and conditions.\r\n     3. Propose acceptance: propose_cluster_action('cluster1', 'accept', <summary>). This sets hubAcceptsClient and approves the pending join CSRs, but applies nothing yet.\r\n     4. Give the operator the proposal id, ask them to run `ocm-mcp approve <id>`, and wait for the token.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Call apply_cluster_action with the token, then verify with get_cluster and get_addon_health that the cluster becomes Available and its agents register.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: addon_troubleshoot\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: addon_troubleshoot\u001b[0m\r\n     The 'governance-policy-framework' add-on looks unhealthy somewhere in the fleet. Investigate without changing anything:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call get_addon_health to find every cluster where an add-on is Degraded or not Available, and confirm which clusters have 'governance-policy-framework' unhealthy.\r\n     2. For each affected cluster, call list_addons_for_cluster(cluster) for the add-on's install namespace and conditions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Call list_cluster_management_addons to read the fleet-level install strategy for 'governance-policy-framework'.\r\n     4. If a spoke context is configured, use get_cluster_health, query_events, and get_pod_logs in the add-on's install namespace to find the root cause.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Report the affected cluste\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: hosted_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: hosted_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n     Assess the health of hosted cluster 'demo-hcp'. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call list_hosted_clusters to locate it and read its version and conditions. If the HostedCluster API is not on this hub, the HCP is hosted elsewhere - fall back to the ManagedCluster view with get_cluster('demo-hcp') and get_cluster_info('demo-hcp').\r\n     2. Call get_hosted_cluster(name, namespace) for its version history, control-plane conditions, and node pools.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Check the NodePools' desired vs current replicas for capacity or scaling problems.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Cross-check the spoke side: get_cluster('demo-hcp') for hub availability and get_addon_health for its add-ons.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Summarize: control-plane state, worker capacity, and anything degraded,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: policy_compliance_report\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: policy_compliance_report\u001b[0m\r\n     Produce a governance compliance report for the fleet. Reads only:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call list_policy_violations for every NonCompliant or Pending policy-cluster pair.\r\n     2. Call list_policies for the full picture, including which policies are inform vs enforce (remediationAction).\r\n     3. Group the violations by policy and by cluster; call out anything Pending separately from NonCompliant.\r\n     4. For the highest-impact violations, note whether the policy is inform (visibility only) or enforce (actively remediating).\r\n     5. Present a concise table and a short prioritized list of what to fix first. Propose no changes - this is a report.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: capacity_report\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: capacity_report\u001b[0m\r\n     Report on fleet capacity so an operator can place new workloads well. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_clusters for each cluster's capacity and availability.\r\n     2. Call get_cluster on the candidates to compare capacity against allocatable.\r\n     3. Where available, call get_cluster_info for node counts and per-node capacity, and list_addon_placement_scores for any custom scores prioritizers use.\r\n     4. Rank clusters by headroom; flag any that are Unavailable, cordoned (NoSelect taint), or nearly full.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Recommend where a new workload should land, and note any cluster that needs attention before it can take more.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: rollout_status\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: rollout_status\u001b[0m\r\n     Report the rollout status of ManifestWorkReplicaSet 'demo-mwrs' in namespace 'default'. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_manifestworkreplicasets to read its summary (total / applied / available / progressing / degraded) and conditions.\r\n     2. Identify the Placement it targets, then call get_placement_decision to list the clusters in scope.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. For any cluster that looks stuck, call get_manifestwork(cluster, <name>) to read the per-resource conditions and status feedback and find what is blocking Apply/Available.\r\n     4. Summarize progress across the fleet and name the specific clusters and resources that are not yet healthy, with evidence.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mlist_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProposals still awaiting human approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: list_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n     []\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe append-only log of every tool call so far - the agent writes its incident report from this record, not from memory.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n     [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"apply_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"88d7cbe34dee4fd9bdbe7ca136dd9767\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 7, \"ts\": 1785215387.0151522, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:49503\", \"seq\": 15, \"prev\": \"2606675100fc9f4f69845fc460bffc48d032285950ec3c2484e337bc42e0647e\", \"hash\": \"dfc91d1f0260e7de5b452d2a3890837ddc319a7ee5e83edc7d6e3ef58b2e3b4e\"},\r\n     {\"tool\": \"propose_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"action\": \"accept\", \"summary\": \"accept (gated, idempotent)\", \"params_json\": \"{}\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 6, \"ts\": 1785215387.023635, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:49503\", \"seq\": 16, \"prev\": \"dfc91d1f0260e7de5b452d2a3890837ddc319a7ee5e83edc7d6e3ef58b2e3b4e\", \"hash\": \"2986f8f6226d0bf0a9aca3503f8643e0e89038e70158090a9e18d2eb1fe18302\"},\r\n     {\"tool\": \"apply_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"38f130b461b4466290f92ae7457d34fa\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 7, \"ts\": 1785215387.031"]
